[{"sha":"01ff6cae883fe8ff523cd9077f9aeb0d7ffc10d0","node_id":"C_kwDOEFLz89oAKDAxZmY2Y2FlODgzZmU4ZmY1MjNjZDkwNzdmOWFlYjBkN2ZmYzEwZDA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/git/commits/01ff6cae883fe8ff523cd9077f9aeb0d7ffc10d0","html_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/commit/01ff6cae883fe8ff523cd9077f9aeb0d7ffc10d0","author":{"name":"Andrey Bobelev","email":"andrey@bobelev.com","date":"2025-11-04T05:18:51Z"},"committer":{"name":"Andrey Bobelev","email":"andrey@bobelev.com","date":"2025-11-04T05:52:29Z"},"tree":{"sha":"b6833ff54997a190eaf6bc19433541a4d06a83db","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/git/trees/b6833ff54997a190eaf6bc19433541a4d06a83db"},"message":"fix: make state cookies valid when client uses multiple login URLs\n\nOn Windows, if the user clicks the Tailscale icon in the system tray,\nit opens a login URL in the browser.\n\nWhen the login URL is opened, `state/nonce` cookies are set for that particular URL.\n\nIf the user clicks the icon again, a new login URL is opened in the browser,\nand new cookies are set.\n\nIf the user proceeds with auth in the first tab,\nthe redirect results in a \"state did not match\" error.\n\nThis patch ensures that each opened login URL sets an individual cookie\nthat remains valid on the `/oidc/callback` page.\n\n`TestOIDCMultipleOpenedLoginUrls` illustrates and tests this behavior.","parents":[{"sha":"2024219bd10adbb5c0d29f900ed0961ace8cc15c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/git/commits/2024219bd10adbb5c0d29f900ed0961ace8cc15c","html_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/commit/2024219bd10adbb5c0d29f900ed0961ace8cc15c"}],"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQIzBAABCAAdFiEETsg2zODHWfdLQs6Li8B/uf6u72MFAmkJlJ8ACgkQi8B/uf6u\n72MIng//Td6mq7shd5YVBVsr+HNBHv7pOH23OrF0nMLbV3QqaDdTXUzc2KUf9h/4\n98KrlOlsp8wFW2lKu9G0/Dj1k6R6z78cNwctPT0NGQX4JdyZ14Th3vBoKPjAOAQH\n0LVejXmMsQOLX4modPPcaWCmOSAc9a0wUDfTI2evlAcccxR9+doV25Vnd/+0de3D\n6p2hetaIQBi85SNhfqm+5rwdkOtzr1yUBx9AYQOMewu5Q3HkD+w0IkvJugSSK9gS\n5pQPFj6cB/4Lr+d+JvDDhbKv25jMkVPXvlznsSkoiZ0KgLuKKoSWh/nXKrEoRT30\n8CxO02o1Tshn7PO06obyWxYPxYgGsiZV09a51yf6FAfMUaxY8s05vx9c3FwuEISk\ng30dNqJgEkvfU/kPgRWNiXRJia2zzPjF/RHk+HxSEHGNltJah7pJf40pDvmDQ9W6\nvlPUnefhpQGOIM1UqJKiEqR9rN+3XYAw9PXrTD7wC2XVJScHNRHFunBuJiP0b8U3\nu9hb5UscQpoAgJuc11rp5FCc13+rLwmffab9Tc0QAhBiG+yJN5FgmFauDybtcHmB\nuxncpzmcVIDhhdzjRSJ3rxg8Co4YrxxUksPy//3CZA1pV2BbwJSvr9NkeU4BT5ph\nIuhq14g/5WSG6iZK/An6EJBY20/JStx9U3X83u0i5/buFfIyzls=\n=gjNF\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","payload":"tree b6833ff54997a190eaf6bc19433541a4d06a83db\nparent 2024219bd10adbb5c0d29f900ed0961ace8cc15c\nauthor Andrey Bobelev <andrey@bobelev.com> 1762233531 +0200\ncommitter Andrey Bobelev <andrey@bobelev.com> 1762235549 +0200\n\nfix: make state cookies valid when client uses multiple login URLs\n\nOn Windows, if the user clicks the Tailscale icon in the system tray,\nit opens a login URL in the browser.\n\nWhen the login URL is opened, `state/nonce` cookies are set for that particular URL.\n\nIf the user clicks the icon again, a new login URL is opened in the browser,\nand new cookies are set.\n\nIf the user proceeds with auth in the first tab,\nthe redirect results in a \"state did not match\" error.\n\nThis patch ensures that each opened login URL sets an individual cookie\nthat remains valid on the `/oidc/callback` page.\n\n`TestOIDCMultipleOpenedLoginUrls` illustrates and tests this behavior.\n","verified_at":"2025-11-04T05:54:20Z"},"event":"committed"},{"id":20692167477,"node_id":"RRE_lADOEFLz887VrKwhzwAAAATRWWs1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/events/20692167477","actor":{"login":"bobelev","id":3942342,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5NDIzNDI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3942342?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bobelev","html_url":"https://github.com/bobelev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bobelev/followers"